                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                        "entry_id": "425a0223-b08e-308b-9b88-7c39d29ceb0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To mislead."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "humorous",
                            "nonstandard",
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "32a5f613-295d-4820-8147-cde311ddca00",
                                "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                                "text": "I think Caspari has been misling you somewhat on the subject of Scenedesmus: the cells divide essentially as in Chlorella, but stay in 4 or 8-celled colonies until the next division."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "33d4f172-d755-4b11-9007-5f2b4c18f217",
                                "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                                "text": "The conduct of the agency coupled with the D. C. Office of Personnel amounts to misling [sic] the appellant as to her [sic] appeal rights to detrimentally rely upon the conduct of her [sic] agency."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ecdb03c-a54e-427d-9ec1-683b1c3fc725",
                                "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                                "text": "Very early I had a relationship to the language of transgression and subversion. i was not as precocious. when i was younger i didn't know when i was on the wrong side of the Law. my errors, my subversions, were unconscious, secreted and embraced somehow by my skin, nerves, blood, a body theatened by language which was slowly misling it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a78a62a-2fb6-417b-b2a1-17984130aee1",
                                "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                                "text": "You're comparing calls for service to patrolling as a security guard, you know it and you should be ashamed for misling and lying."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f529b89-6c7c-4c96-97a0-9eb308429b5d",
                                "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                                "text": "So Gordon Ramsay is misling his entire American audience? They never actually discuss the \"garnish,\" but on the rare occasions when he yells at someone for screwing up a \"garnish,\" it's always a potato or vegetable."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f5b7113e-8d52-4554-8eb7-647523fe8f68",
                                "sense_id": "4d628a89-fdf2-3e9b-af92-242c559ba0c0",
                                "text": "Once again youse guys were misling me with \"Asian\" -- I wondered whether it might relate somehow to Singapore-Chinese \"la,\" which serves a similar function."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
